(1506, 'posts', 49, 'en', NULL, 'Comprehensive guide to buying a kalimba | Review of 2 types of kalimba design | A very attractive and simple instrument to learn', NULL, 'This article introduces the kalimba and provides a comprehensive buying guide. The kalimba is a small, lightweight, and melodic instrument of African origin, consisting of a wooden or glass body and metal tines. It is easy to learn, making it ideal for beginners.\n\nWhen buying a kalimba, important factors include material, number of tines, build quality, size, and weight. Wooden kalimbas produce louder, richer sounds and allow techniques like vibrato, while glass kalimbas are more visually appealing and produce softer tones but with lower volume.\n\nOther key considerations include tuning (commonly C major), tine count (typically 17 for versatility), and the presence of a resonance hole. Proper maintenance—such as avoiding impact, humidity, and extreme temperatures—is also essential.\n\nOverall, the kalimba is an affordable, portable, and beginner-friendly instrument that can be learned quickly, and choosing the right one depends on your needs, preferences, and budget.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>In this article from <a href=\"https://sornaz.com/\">Sornaz</a>, we intend to introduce you to the new and highly attractive instrument called the kalimba, and also provide the necessary guidance and tips for <strong><span style=\"color: #0000ff;\">buying a kalimba</span></strong> so that you can make your purchase with greater care and precision.</p>\n\n<h2>Introduction to the Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>The kalimba is a very simple, beautiful, pleasant-sounding, and lightweight instrument. Playing musical pieces on this instrument, whose main origin is the African continent, is a truly wonderful experience, and learning to play it is also very easy.</p>\n\n<p>The structure of the kalimba consists of a wooden or glass body and several metal tines (keys). The number of these tines varies in different sizes and dimensions of the kalimba, and the very pleasant sound is produced by the vibration of these tines.</p>\n\n<p>It should be noted that to amplify and strengthen the sound of the kalimba, there is a sound hole in the center of the instrument.</p>\n\n<p>Because the kalimba is played by striking the tines with the fingers, it is also known as the African piano or finger piano, and the metal tines of this instrument are actually equivalent to the keys on a piano.</p>\n\n<p>If you are not familiar with this instrument and this is the first time you intend to purchase a kalimba, please continue with us so that we can provide you with the important points for buying and acquiring a kalimba.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Should You Buy a Kalimba? Reasons for Buying a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>First, we must answer this important question: why do we want to buy a kalimba?</p>\n\n<p>The kalimba is a very attractive and lovable instrument with a highly pleasant sound, which is why it has gained many fans all over the world.</p>\n\n<p>Another reason is that you do not need to attend courses or classes to learn the kalimba, and you can easily learn to play it at home with practice, and quite quickly.</p>\n\n<p>Moreover, because of its small size, you can carry it with you wherever you want.</p>\n\n<p>In terms of price, it is also cheaper than other instruments, and if you intend to learn an easy and relaxing instrument, you can purchase a kalimba at an affordable price and start playing it.</p>\n\n<p>The most important point when buying a kalimba is the feeling of comfort when holding the instrument and playing it.</p>\n\n<h2>Material, Weight, and Standard Size of the Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>The kalimba is standardly designed in approximately 13 × 18 cm dimensions with a height of about 3 cm, and in its standard form, it weighs between 200 and 300 grams. Before buying a kalimba, you should keep in mind that the kalimba, like any other instrument, has undergone changes and is also made in other dimensions and weights. Even its body material, which is traditionally made of wood, has in recent years, according to the taste of designers, sometimes been made of glass as well.</p>\n\n<p>Kalimbas with glass bodies, because they lack a sound box, have a weaker sound compared to traditional kalimbas with wooden bodies. Therefore, whether to buy a glass or wooden kalimba depends on your own preference — whether you want the louder sound of a wooden kalimba or the stunning beauty of a glass kalimba.</p>\n\n<p>One of the most important points in buying a kalimba is examining the quality of the instrument’s design and materials, because it helps you in maintaining the instrument and also affects the quality of the sound produced.</p>\n\n<p>For traditional kalimbas, which are a combination of metal and wood, it is recommended that the wood used be from trees such as mulberry, maple, or walnut to provide better quality.</p>\n\n<p>Regarding glass kalimbas, their fragility is a negative point, so more care must be taken in maintaining and preserving them compared to wooden ones.</p>\n\n<p>The number of metal tines on a kalimba is 7 in some models and more than that in others. How many tines your instrument should have depends on your skill, experience, and proficiency in playing the kalimba. If you are currently at the beginning of learning and playing the kalimba, we suggest you purchase an instrument with fewer tines.</p>\n\n[caption id=\"attachment_3419\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"800\"]<img class=\"wp-image-3419 size-full\" src=\"https://sornaz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/hluru-17-key-flat-board-kalimba-thumb-piano-bearfawn-transparent-acrylic-single-board-c-tone-kalimba-instrument-misoundofnature-1.webp\" alt=\"Glass Kalimba\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /> Glass Kalimba[/caption]\n\n<h2>Construction Style – An Important Point When Buying a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>Currently, there is a great variety in the construction styles of kalimbas in the market, and there are many options to choose from when buying a kalimba. Among different kalimbas, some models may have different tines and bodies compared to others. In fact, it is the construction style of the kalimba that distinguishes one from another and causes differences in the materials used and even in the sound quality of the kalimba.</p>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, one of the most important points you will probably encounter is that some kalimbas have sound holes and others do not. The holes placed on kalimbas enhance and especially increase the volume of the sound; these are also called sound boxes. Kalimbas with solid bodies usually produce less sound. Keep in mind that the material of the kalimba is also very important in this regard, and kalimbas with wooden bodies generally produce a higher quality and louder sound than glass kalimbas.</p>\n\n<h2>The Best Type of Wood for Making a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>The kalimba is usually made of wood. Of course, nowadays many types of crystal kalimbas have also entered the market that have very diverse and interesting designs, but if sound quality is more important to you than the appearance of the instrument, it is better to choose a wooden kalimba.</p>\n\n<p>The type and kind of wood used in making a kalimba has a great and direct impact on sound quality, tone, and durability. In general, the harder and stronger the wood, the better the sound quality of the kalimba will be, because this causes better reflection of sound waves.</p>\n\n<p>A traditional kalimba is made from hard African wood (usually kiaat). However, today many alternatives have replaced this model because finding kiaat wood is very difficult and practically almost impossible for other countries. Therefore, the best woods for making a kalimba can be one of the following options:</p>\n\n<p>Sandalwood, mahogany, coconut, gourd, bamboo, spruce, maple, walnut, rosewood, birch, camphor, koa.</p>\n\n<h2>The Tone Color of the Kalimba – An Important Point When Buying a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, you should keep in mind that a glass kalimba, due to its lower volume, will have a softer sound, which is ideal for calm and low-movement songs, especially lullabies or songs for meditation.</p>\n\n<p>On the other hand, a wooden kalimba has a louder and brighter sound, which is why it is more interesting for popular songs that are usually accompanied by lyrics.</p>\n\n<h3>Vibrato on the Kalimba</h3>\n\n<p>Vibrato refers to a continuous and subtle change in the pitch level of the instrument that occurs directly above and below the main note and gives the music a beautiful effect.</p>\n\n<p>Vibrato cannot be produced on glass kalimbas. Some wooden kalimbas, especially those with sound holes, can cause the sound to vibrate; these instruments have additional holes on the back that the player can open and close while playing to create vibration in the sound. Vibrato is a very beautiful and simple feature that makes the sound coming from the kalimba more flexible and adds depth and feeling to the performer’s playing.</p>\n\n<h2>Tuning the Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba — an instrument originating from the African continent — a case and a special tuning hammer are delivered to the buyer. To tune the kalimba, you must strike the tines up and down with the hammer so that they move slightly backward or forward and your kalimba becomes tuned.</p>\n\n<p>In practice, when you strike the tines of your instrument, you change the vibrating length of the tines relative to the bridge of the instrument. Therefore, a higher sound is produced from a tine with a shorter vibrating length, while the longer the vibrating length of the tine, the lower the sound produced will be.</p>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, to make sure of the correct position and size of the tines and the tuning of the kalimba, you can use an electronic tuner or tuning apps installed on your mobile phone.</p>\n\n<p>When the note color on the tuner screen is red, it indicates that the frequency is wrong or that tine is out of tune. You must move the tines with the hammer until the desired note color turns green. If you want the sound of your instrument to be lower, strike the hammer on the upper part of the tines; a higher sound is achieved by striking the lower part of the tines.</p>\n\n<h2>Tuning (Key) of the Kalimba Has a Great Impact on Buying a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>Before buying a kalimba, one of the first things you should decide on is the tuning or key of the kalimba — that is, decide how you want to tune and set your kalimba. To make this decision, two issues should be considered:</p>\n\n<p>If you want to play familiar and well-known songs — that is, songs that are heard a lot in public places — you should tune your kalimba in **diatonic** mode. This word may sound a bit complicated, but it has a very simple meaning.</p>\n\n<p>For this purpose, we should take a look at the keys of a piano. The white keys of the piano produce diatonic notes.</p>\n\n[caption id=\"attachment_3778\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"1010\"]<img class=\"wp-image-3778 size-full\" src=\"https://sornaz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/sornaz_piano_keys.png\" alt=\"Piano Keys\" width=\"1010\" height=\"274\" /> Piano Keys[/caption]\n\n<p>In most musical pieces and Western instruments over the past 200–300 years, chromatic scales have been used. If you look again at the piano keys in the image above, there are twelve keys or notes in each octave (the interval between two consecutive notes of the same name with different frequencies) — from C to B — of which seven are white keys and five are black keys. In fact, in chromatic scales, the notes of the black keys are also added to your tuning.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, to make things as simple as possible, you can think of the diatonic scale as simply having the seven white piano keys, and the most advanced kalimbas are tuned in this way!</p>\n\n<p>If the piece or song you have chosen to play requires chromatic tuning (the notes of the black piano keys), you only need to use the small hammer provided in the kalimba packaging to tune the tines of your kalimba to correspond to the black piano keys.</p>\n\n<p>On the other hand, beginners may wonder how their kalimba should be tuned and what key it should have. In answer to this question, it should be said that the “C” or “Do” tuning is the most common international standard for this instrument.</p>\n\n<p>The tuning chart for the tines of a kalimba tuned in C Major is as follows:</p>\n\n[caption id=\"attachment_3780\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"955\"]<img class=\"wp-image-3780 size-full\" src=\"https://sornaz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/sornaz_calimba_tuning_keys.jpg\" alt=\"Kalimba Tine Tuning Chart in C Major\" width=\"955\" height=\"494\" /> Kalimba Tine Tuning Chart in C Major[/caption]\n\n<h2>Examining the Functionality of Kalimba Tines and Introducing Different Types</h2>\n\n<p>The tines of a kalimba refer to the metal strips on the kalimba that are responsible for producing sound. The sound produced by playing on the kalimba tines is soft, but with their pleasant tone, they easily captivate listeners.</p>\n\n<p>The tines of a kalimba are usually made of metals such as: stainless steel, recycled steel, and spring steel.</p>\n\n<h3>Number of Tines</h3>\n\n<p>Most modern kalimbas have 17 tines. Some others have 10, 12, or 15 tines. Sometimes models with 7 or 8 tines are also made, which are usually not used for playing popular songs but are very relaxing.</p>\n\n<p>If you are undecided between buying a 15-tine or 17-tine kalimba, you should keep in mind that there is not much difference between these kalimbas. The two extra notes you get from the 17-tine version are rarely used, but having them when needed is definitely good.</p>\n\n<h3>Color Labels</h3>\n\n<p>To increase playing speed and make note identification easier, when buying a kalimba, a number of colored stickers representing musical notes are provided with the instrument. The note names are written in English on them, and they are stuck on the tines of the instrument. Although you can purchase these stickers separately, it is better if they are included with the product when buying the kalimba.</p>\n\n<h2>Buying an Authentic Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>The kalimba is produced in different shapes, sizes, tone colors, and materials, and various types are also available in the Iranian market. To buy a perfect kalimba, you need to follow this buying guide. By knowing these points, you can choose the most suitable type of kalimba that best meets your needs according to your budget.</p>\n\n<p>Here it is necessary to point out that there is no such thing as an “authentic” or “original” kalimba! Saying “buy an original kalimba” is like saying “buy an original piano or guitar”! Like all other instruments, the kalimba is produced under different brands and with different qualities and offered in the market. In this article, we will teach you the essential points for choosing a kalimba so that you can make the best possible choice according to your budget.</p>\n\n<h2>The Best Types of Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, keep in mind that the best types and models of kalimba are categorized into three main types: Celeste, Treble, and Alto:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Celeste-type kalimbas are mounted on a board and have clear high notes; compared to other types, they look more delicate.</li>\n  <li>Treble-type kalimbas have 17 notes.</li>\n  <li>The Alto model also has 15 notes, which is exactly two octaves.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Important Points for Buying a Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, you should pay special attention to the following points to make the best possible choice:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Because the <strong>kalimba</strong> must be held in the hand while playing, the lighter its weight, the better when buying a kalimba.</li>\n  <li>Pay attention to the fact that sometimes too many tines make the instrument larger, making it difficult to reach all of them while playing.</li>\n  <li>It is recommended to use common kalimbas that are more popular, because their tutorials are more accessible and playing them is simpler. For example, the 17-tine or 17-key kalimba is more common.</li>\n  <li>Learning and training to play the kalimba is not difficult, and you can easily learn to play the kalimba, but it requires concentration and practice.</li>\n  <li>When buying a kalimba, it should be provided to you in its special carrying case, along with a hammer and usually colored stickers.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Caring for Your Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>After buying a kalimba, another important issue arises — caring for the instrument — and you should observe the following points:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Avoid strong impacts on the instrument or shaking it vigorously.</li>\n  <li>Like all other wooden instruments, do not place the kalimba in hot environments, as this can loosen the glue of the body.</li>\n  <li>Contraction and expansion will cause the body of the instrument to crack; on the other hand, it will disrupt the performance of the tines and change the tuning. Therefore, protect the instrument from heat and cold.</li>\n  <li>Do not place the kalimba in humid places, because moisture has a negative effect on wood.</li>\n  <li>When you are not using the instrument, be sure to place it in its special carrying case and <strong>use the case for storage and transport</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Is Learning to Play the Kalimba Difficult?</h2>\n\n<p>Learning and training to play the <strong>kalimba</strong> is not difficult. Certainly, if you have the necessary interest in this instrument and its sound, you can easily learn to play this pleasant instrument. There are many in-person and online tutorials available for learning to play the kalimba, with the help of which you can learn this instrument very quickly. Many beginners can easily play simple and short songs on the kalimba with just a few weeks of practice.</p>\n\n<p>You should keep in mind that if you are really interested in playing the kalimba, with a lot of practice and perseverance, you can learn to play the kalimba very quickly. The length of time it takes to **learn the kalimba** depends on your level of interest and effort and can be very short.</p>\n\n<h2>Playing the Kalimba</h2>\n\n<p>Playing wooden kalimbas, paying attention to the points mentioned in this kalimba buying guide — especially its weight and sound volume — will be much simpler for beginners. If you do not want to put too much pressure on your wrist and fingers while playing the kalimba and cause pain, choose wooden kalimbas. The use of a glass kalimba is recommended only when you already have experience playing a wooden kalimba.</p>\n\n<p>In the following, we will examine the advantages and disadvantages of wooden and glass kalimbas so that you can make your <a href=\"https://sornaz.com/category/%d8%ae%d8%b1%db%8c%d8%af-%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%b2/\">instrument purchase</a> with more information.</p>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<h3>What Are the Most Important Advantages and Disadvantages of Buying a Glass Kalimba?</h3>\n\n<h4><strong>Advantages:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>The warmer tone and character of glass kalimbas can be more suitable for certain songs and styles.</li>\n  <li>They have more variety in design and appearance and are usually more beautiful visually than wooden instruments.</li>\n  <li>The softer sound of wooden kalimbas is more suitable for practice because it will not disturb others.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4><strong>Disadvantages:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>They are usually heavier than the wooden type and may put more pressure on the wrist during long playing sessions.</li>\n  <li>The lower volume of glass kalimbas can sometimes be considered a disadvantage because to produce a stronger sound, you have to strike the tines with more force.</li>\n  <li>Glass kalimbas are more prone to scratches and damage than wooden kalimbas.</li>\n  <li>The glass type is usually more expensive than wooden kalimbas due to its more beautiful appearance.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>What Are the Most Important Advantages and Disadvantages of Buying a Wooden Kalimba?</h3>\n\n<h4><strong>Advantages:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>The lighter weight of a wooden kalimba makes holding the kalimba and playing it for long periods much easier.</li>\n  <li>The tone and sound character of wooden kalimbas is more traditional.</li>\n  <li>Performing more advanced techniques such as vibrato is possible on these types of instruments.</li>\n  <li>They have less fragility compared to the glass type.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4><strong>Disadvantages:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>There is less variety in design and appearance in this model.</li>\n  <li>They have a stronger tone, which may not be very desirable for performing soft songs.</li>\n  <li>Their loud sound may be problematic when those around need silence and calm.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>What Can Be Said About Using Both Glass and Wooden Kalimbas at the Same Time?</h3>\n\n<p>Many kalimba players like to use both glass and wooden kalimbas. Having both types allows you to experience more different tone colors and discover more flexibility in the sounds. If you pay attention to the subtle difference in the sound of these two models, you can notice which type of kalimba gives a better sound for each song.</p>\n\n<p>When buying a kalimba, keep this point in mind: consider having two kalimbas only after you have already practiced with one of them. If you intend to play the kalimba for the first time, choose only one model to buy, because until you have tried playing it, you will not know whether you will want to continue playing this instrument or not. Of course, if you have no problem with the budget, having both types of instruments is fine, and because of the relatively low price of this instrument, even if you later decide not to continue playing it, you will not suffer much financially from buying a kalimba.</p>\n\n&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n\n<p>If you have any comments or questions regarding buying a kalimba, please share them in the comments section of the article with us to improve the quality of this educational content.</p>', '2023-09-06 22:31:11', 0, '2025-02-14 01:00:32', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1507, 'posts', 50, 'en', NULL, 'Comprehensive guide to buying a hang drum | 4 important tips for purchasing a hang drum for beginners and professionals', NULL, 'This article introduces the handpan (hang drum) and provides a comprehensive buying guide. The handpan is a melodic percussion instrument made of two metal shells and played with the hands. It produces soft, soothing sounds that create a relaxing and meditative atmosphere, which has made it increasingly popular in recent years.\n\nLearning the handpan is relatively easy, especially for beginners, due to its limited number of notes. The learning time depends on factors such as practice, rhythm understanding, and access to proper instruction.\n\nWhen buying a handpan, important considerations include sound quality and tuning accuracy, build quality, durability, note sustain, and brand reliability. The material (such as stainless steel, raw steel, or nitrided steel) and size (commonly 18 or 22 inches) also affect sound and playability.\n\nOther key factors include setting a budget, ensuring value for money, testing the instrument before purchase, and consulting an expert if needed. Ultimately, choosing a high-quality handpan can provide a highly enjoyable and rewarding musical experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p>In this article from the <a href=\"https://sornaz.com/\">Sornaz Music School</a>, we intend to introduce you to one of the most attractive instruments in the world and provide a guide for <span style=\"color: #0000ff;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #0000ff;\">buying a hang drum</span></strong></span>, a very pleasant instrument that has countless fans around the world and their number is increasing day by day. Therefore, we will try to familiarize you with the features of the hang drum and provide a comprehensive guide for buying a hang drum so that by studying it, you can prepare this attractive instrument as quickly as possible and start playing the hang drum.</p>\n<h2>Introduction to the Hang Drum</h2>\n<p>The hang drum is one of the most popular instruments in the world today, which, due to its very soft and gentle sound, creates a highly calming and nostalgic atmosphere when playing, which is why it has gained a huge number of fans in the last decade.</p>\n<p>The hang drum, which is also known by the names “handpan” or “hang,” is a self-sounding melodic percussion instrument. You can play this instrument without using any tools and only by striking it with your hands and enjoy listening to the melody you create. The sound is extremely pleasant and calming.</p>\n<p>The hang drum is made of two curved metal plates that are symmetrically joined together. It is made from a square steel sheet with dimensions of 68 cm², of which the manufacturers use 57 cm of the central space of this square as the main body of the instrument, and 5.4 cm of the edge and margin of the steel sheet is used for gluing the two shells together, which has no effect on the tuning of the instrument.</p>\n<p>The hang drum maker first shapes the steel sheet into a smooth and uniform curved and bowl shape using a hydroforming machine so that the shell becomes a hemisphere with a diameter of 57 cm and a depth of 15 cm.</p>\n<p>On the upper curve, the locations of the notes are created, which is called the ding side. The lower curve, which is called the gu side, has a hole in its center. On the outer side of the hang drum, a plastic sheath is installed that acts as a damper (sound reducer or muffler).</p>\n<p>If the player wishes, they can remove this plastic sheath from their instrument to receive a fuller sound and higher <a href=\"https://fa.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D8%AA%D8%B4%D8%AF%DB%8C%D8%AF_(%D9%81%DB%8C%D8%B2%DB%8C%DA%A9)\">resonance</a> from the instrument.</p>\n<p>In its natural and standard state, the hang drum has eight notes, one of which is used as the main note or ding, but recently, hang drum makers have made changes and innovations in it and have increased the number of hang drum notes to 22, in some cases placing some notes on the lower plate due to the limited space of the instrument.</p>\n[caption id=\"attachment_3468\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"300\"]<img class=\"wp-image-3468 size-full\" src=\"https://sornaz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/5c576bd4c0894b1255230fe52855ee64a1bc28e3_1661595727.jpg\" alt=\"Hang drum, a very popular instrument in the world\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" /> The hang drum is one of the most popular instruments in the world in the 21st century.[/caption]\n<h3>Is Learning to Play the Hang Drum Difficult?</h3>\n<p>Playing the <strong>hang drum</strong> is not as difficult as it seems. After buying a hang drum, if you put in enough effort and have interest, you can easily learn to play the hang drum. Playing the hang drum is not more difficult than other instruments. On the other hand, if you understand rhythm in music, using this instrument will be much simpler.</p>\n<h3>How Long Does It Take to Learn to Play the Hang Drum?</h3>\n<p>One of the questions that arises when buying a hang drum is how long it takes to learn to play this instrument. The duration of learning to play the hang drum is mostly an individual matter, and multiple factors affect learning. For example, each person has a different understanding of rhythm. On the other hand, not all of us have the same amount of free time for learning how to play the hang drum, and each person dedicates a different amount of time per day to learning the hang drum depending on their age, job, and personal concerns. Each person has a different learning speed compared to another person, and we do not all use the same type and quality of instrument.</p>\n<p>Apart from the mentioned cases, there is a big difference between someone who works alone and self-taught and a person who attends classes and benefits from the help of a professional instructor. However, the hang drum is among the group of instruments whose playing is much simpler to learn than instruments such as guitar and piano.</p>\n<p>The most important reason for the simplicity of playing the hang drum is the number of its notes, since this instrument has far fewer notes than other instruments. Therefore, for beginners and new players, playing it is simpler than most instruments. If you have previously had experience playing another <strong>percussion instrument</strong> or have a good understanding of rhythm in music, becoming an outstanding hang drum player will be a very simple task for you.</p>\n<h2>Necessary and Essential Points for Preparing and Buying a Hang Drum</h2>\n<p>The hang drum, due to the large number of fans it has found in our country, is offered in the market with various qualities and prices, which increases the possible choices for buying a hang drum and makes the <a href=\"https://sornaz.com/category/%d8%ae%d8%b1%db%8c%d8%af-%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%b2/\">instrument buying</a> process a bit difficult. Now, in this section, we want to mention the points you should observe when buying a hang drum so that you can prepare a hang drum with a better perspective:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Before buying a hang drum, play all parts of the ding of the instrument and check all the notes with the help of a tuner. When examining the notes of the hang drum with the tuner, you should keep in mind that a difference of one to two cents of the notes with a 440 Hz tuner is natural and this difference is not perceptible to the human ear. Because melodic percussion instruments are not tuned based on the Pythagorean tuning system, and therefore the intervals between the notes may be slightly different from the global tuning system. But be sure to check that the sound is not excessively out of tune. If the sound is out of tune, avoid buying the hang drum.</li>\n  <li>Check the part where the steel plates of the hang drum are joined together. There should be no distortion, unevenness, dirty or incorrect connection, seams, grooves, or such occurrences in the connection parts of the hang drum. In any instrument, connections are the most important parts. Since the hang drum is a metal instrument, the existence of any seam or groove may allow moisture to enter the instrument over time and cause the instrument to go out of tune or become unusable in any way.</li>\n  <li>Play all the notes on the hang drum. The sustain of the notes and the quality of the sound of the notes indicate the health of the instrument. If the sustain of the note is too short or too long, it means that the instrument has not been properly adjusted and will soon go out of tune. Also, an excessively sharp or overly muddy and dull sound indicates incorrect and poor craftsmanship.</li>\n  <li>Check the bottom of the hang drum, where it is placed on the stand or foot; it must be completely smooth and flat. The existence of any unevenness, dents, darkening, or dullness indicates that the material and craftsmanship used in the construction of the hang drum instrument are unhealthy and of low quality.</li>\n  <li>Be sure to check the brand and model of the instrument and make sure that fake material is not sold to you instead of original and genuine material under the name of reputable brands.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What Is the Reason for the Extreme Popularity of the Hang Drum?</h2>\n<p>These days, the <strong>hang drum</strong> has become one of the most popular and best-selling musical instruments for various reasons, and its popularity is increasing day by day. First of all, the simplicity of learning the hang drum makes it possible for anyone to quickly acquire the ability to play it. The hang drum is considered a relatively new instrument, and therefore there are still no strict instructions regarding the correct way to play this instrument.</p>\n<p>On the other hand, it is essential to pay attention to the fact that the hang drum and the tongue drum are not the same. Tongue drums are usually intended for calm and soothing playing and for meditation. On the other hand, hang drums are made from various materials and offer a range of different styles from calm meditation to fast playing in enclosed spaces.</p>\n&nbsp;\n<h2>What Factors Affect the Sound Quality of the Hang Drum?</h2>\n<p>When buying a hang drum, you should know that for easier management and maintenance of this instrument, learning how to use it and playing the instrument is not enough. Before buying a hang drum, you must have more information about this instrument. This information, in addition to awareness of the different parts of the instrument and the quality of the materials used in its production, also includes knowledge of sound quality and factors affecting the sound output of the hang drum. The sound of the instrument must be of high quality, and therefore when buying a hang drum, you must know how to recognize it.</p>\n<p>Only in this way will your playing training proceed in the right direction. If you intend to work self-taught, you must know everything about the sound quality of the hang drum, because you do not have a teacher to correct your mistakes.</p>\n<p>A good sound output comes from a precise and correct goal and proper technique. Since the hang drum has a concave shape, this instrument has a hole in its lower part that must always remain open. When playing, you can place the instrument on your legs or put it on a soft surface. If you place the instrument on a very hard surface, the sound output of the instrument will not be good, or the sound will have a dry quality.</p>\n<p>With all these points, everything depends on the type and quality of the sound you want to hear from the hang drum. For example, in playing the hang drum, you can use your hands or custom wooden sticks for striking. These sticks are usually made from pine wood and wrapped in wool. Using these sticks creates more sound than the sound produced by striking the instrument with the hands.</p>\n<h2>What Points Should Be Considered When Buying a Hang Drum for Starting to Learn?</h2>\n<p>Before deciding to prepare and buy a hang drum, several important points regarding buying a hang drum should be kept in mind. With a little research, you will make the right decision. Try to listen a lot to the songs that are played with the hang drum. YouTube can be a good source for listening to and watching hang drum songs and performances.</p>\n<p>In buying a hang drum, considering the quality of the product is very important and vital because low quality will create an unpleasant experience for you and increase the possibility of abandoning this pleasant instrument.</p>\n<p>Due to the very high popularity of the hang drum among students, players, and even people who have no knowledge of music, many sellers and manufacturers of hang drums try to sell this instrument at high prices. So try to calmly and with high precision find a product that is sufficiently suitable and at the same time affordable.</p>\n<p>To ensure buying a suitable hang drum, ask the seller to provide you with explanations about the different parts of the instrument and the quality of the materials used in the construction of the hang drum. This is especially important if the instrument is more expensive. When buying a hang drum, be sure to pay attention to the following points:</p>\n<h3>1. How the Hang Drum Is Made</h3>\n<p>The first point you should pay attention to when buying a hang drum is to first pay attention to how it is made. The hang drum must be strong and stable enough so that you can play it with confidence and without fear of damaging the instrument. A good hang drum must, regardless of whether it is prepared for beginners or professionals, withstand a reasonable amount of playing. Choose a hang drum that is well made and also properly tuned.</p>\n<p>If the main features in the construction of the hang drum are not acceptable, the other capabilities of the hang drum will be ignored. The selected model must be made with an octave and complex fifth harmonies that are tuned on each note.</p>\n[caption id=\"attachment_3783\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"800\"]<img class=\"wp-image-3783 size-full\" src=\"https://sornaz.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/sornaz_hangdrum_notes.jpg\" alt=\"Location of musical notes on the hang drum instrument\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /> Location of musical notes on the hang drum instrument[/caption]\n<h3>2. Suitable Material and Size for Buying a Hang Drum</h3>\n<p>Another important criterion that should be paid attention to when buying a hang drum is the size and material used in the construction of the hang drum. The common size in making a hang drum is 22 inches, but there are also smaller 18-inch hang drums. Larger instruments usually have a more beautiful and pleasant sound, but the main question here is which one is more useful for you? Generally, for beginners and new players, smaller versions are more suitable.</p>\n<p>Another important point in buying a hang drum is that hang drums are usually produced with various materials, which are usually made of steel, and each of them has its own special features and different advantages and disadvantages. The three main types are stainless steel, raw steel, and nitrided steel.</p>\n<h3>3. Ensuring the Quality of the Instrument Compared to the Cost Paid</h3>\n<p>Before buying a hang drum, you must make a decision about your budget. Determine the price range that is reasonable and suitable for you, then look for buying a hang drum that matches your desired price. For this purpose, we suggest that you make every effort to get the best possible quality for the cost paid. Being a beginner and new does not justify buying a bad and poor-quality hang drum.</p>\n<h3>4. Consulting with an Expert Before Buying a Hang Drum</h3>\n<p>You should keep in mind that if you do not have the necessary and sufficient information for recognizing and buying a good hang drum and the points mentioned in this article, which is a buying guide for the hang drum, seem too confusing to you, it is better to consult with a specialist. Experts in this field are well familiar with the instruments, know the advantages and disadvantages of hang drums, and at first glance can tell you whether the hang drum you have in mind has acceptable quality or not, and whether it is worth the cost paid.</p>\n<p></p>', '2023-09-08 22:29:38', 0, '2024-09-18 22:33:50', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
